## Why This Is Asked
This probes practical Azure OpenAI integration with APIM, Functions, Redis, and Table Storage, focusing on latency, data governance, and beginner-friendly design.

## Key Concepts
- API Management gating
- Data redaction
- Redis caching for performance
- Azure Table Storage FAQ catalog
- Latency testing and basic observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Redaction function
function redactPII(text) {
  return text
    .replace(/\b[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\.[A-Z]{2,}\b/gi, "[REDACTED_EMAIL]")
    .replace(/\b\d{3}-\d{2}-\d{4}\b/g, "[REDACTED_SSN]");
}
```

```javascript
// Redis cache lookup
async function getAnswer(query) {
  const key = `faq:${query}`;
  let cached = await redis.get(key);
  if (cached) return JSON.parse(cached);
  const answer = await fetchFromTable(query);
  await redis.set(key, JSON.stringify(answer), { EX: 300 });
  return answer;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test cache eviction and cold-start behavior?
- How would you handle multilingual queries in this flow?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect a multi-tenant Azure OpenAI flow integrated with DevOps, covering data lineage, security, and performance.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI + API Management
- Cognitive Search KB in Blob
- Per-tenant RBAC (Azure AD)
- PII redaction (Text Analytics)
- Data Lake logging
- Canary deployments and end-to-end latency goals

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestration snippet showing tenant context, diff->prompt, and moderation
async function reviewPR(prDiff, tenantId){
  const kb = await loadKB(tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(prDiff, kb, tenantId);
  const review = await openAiReview(prompt);
  if(hasPIIRisk(review)){ redact(review); }
  await storeLogs(tenantId, {prDiff, review});
  return review.comments;
}
``` 

